{"kind":"artifact","text":"The browser refuses a remote carrying a query or fragment as well as one whose scheme is not http or https, deciding both for itself where the href is created. Exact clean pushed head 7da8b753682d38aa118e709943df0ee8c03e5c37; tree 29ac34a8, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's child 48ec44db and my promise ca8d07ed.\n\nProvenance is the only thing that changed since 512f5c5f: byte-identical tree, amended trailer naming the child.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. repoRemoteHref now also declines any URL whose serialisation carries ? or #. Codex found the inconsistency and it was mine: I declined userinfo because it may carry a credential, then passed ?access_token=SECRET through to the DOM and the href. Rejecting is the coherent rule — a repository's own address needs neither component — and judging which parameter names are secret would be an enumerated denylist, the shape the scheme rule deliberately avoids.\n\nTHE TEST IS ON THE SERIALISATION. Both parsers escape ? and # wherever they appear in a host or path, so a bare one in the output can only be the delimiter, including the empty ones search and hash record. A case pins that a percent-encoded ? inside a path stays admitted, so a naive substring check over raw input would fail rather than silently over-refuse.\n\nUNENUMERATED SCHEMES NOW PIN THE ALLOWLIST. future+git:// and x-unheard-of:// parse cleanly with a host, so only the allowlist can refuse them; my earlier org-alias: case could not, having no host. Replacing the allowlist with a denylist fails a rendered-DOM assertion.\n\nONE DIVERGENCE RECORDED. Go drops a bare trailing # and JavaScript keeps it — harmless only because the service now never emits either delimiter, and where they differ the browser is stricter.\n\nGates run by me at this exact head from a clean run I watched exit: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 98/98; gofmt empty; build and vet exit 0; make ui leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"7da8b753682d38aa118e709943df0ee8c03e5c37","path":"ui"}}